.invokeFunction('convertToInteractive',\n","                                                     [key], {});\n","          if (!dataTable) return;\n","\n","          const docLinkHtml = 'Like what you see? Visit the ' +\n","            '<a target=\"_blank\" href=https://colab.research.google.com/notebooks/data_table.ipynb>data table notebook</a>'\n","            + ' to learn more about interactive tables.';\n","          element.innerHTML = '';\n","          dataTable['output_type'] = 'display_data';\n","          await google.colab.output.renderOutput(dataTable, element);\n","          const docLink = document.createElement('div');\n","          docLink.innerHTML = docLinkHtml;\n","          element.appendChild(docLink);\n","        }\n","      </script>\n","    </div>\n","  </div>\n","  "]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":53}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Task 12: Show a Pointplot of Cancellation Rates by Deposit Type"],"metadata":{"id":"bVI55Dw1X8Rf"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Using the created dataframe named `pointplot_data`, create a poinplot using `sns.lineplot` containing the given arguments:\n","- `data`: `pointplot_data`\n","- `x`: `'deposit_type'`\n","- `y`: `'cancel_rate'`\n","- `hue`: `'is_repeated_guest'`\n","- `join`: `False`\n","- `capsize`:`0.1`\n","- `ax`:`ax`\n","\n","Lastly, set the title named `Cancellation Rates by Deposity type and Repeating Guest`, x label named `Deposit Type`, y label named `Cancellation Rate`, the legend title named `Returning Guest`."],"metadata":{"id":"vqWIiHOC9iYO"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Fill in the blanks\n","\n","# fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7,8))\n","# sns.pointplot(data=_______, x='_______', y='_______',\n","#               hue='_______', join=_______,\n","#               capsize=____, ax=___)\n","\n","# ax.set_xlabel('_______')\n","# ax.set_ylabel('______________')\n","# ax.set_title('____________________________')\n","# ax.legend(title='____________________________')"],"metadata":{"id":"dI0tnO9rgLG4"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 8))\n","sns.pointplot(data=pointplot_data, x='deposit_type', y='cancel_rate',\n","              hue='is_repeated_guest', join=False,\n","              capsize=0.1, ax=ax)\n","\n","ax.set_xlabel('Deposit Type')\n","ax.set_ylabel('Cancellation Rate')\n","ax.set_title('Cancellation Rates by Deposit Type and Repeating Guest')\n","ax.legend(title='Returning Guest')"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":735},"id":"_jWOb1VAyWM4","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1685200664839,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":1674,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"ae57427b-7fc2-4f19-afe1-3a9f4c530dbe"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["<matplotlib.legend.Legend at 0x7f8b9afc5de0>"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":54},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 700x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Task 13 (Optional): Other Analysis and Insights"],"metadata":{"id":"QiVxh2HhyOmI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**This portion of the Final Task is not required to answer but it is highly recommended to do so.**\n","\n","For this part, this would be the place where you can provide additional plots, charts, visualizations, and insights that may be interesting into your report. Although, if you have no insights that you want to share, you can skip to the next part (\"Conclusions and Recommendations\").\n","\n","You may add code or text cells by pointing your mouse to the end of a code cell and click \"Code\" or \"Text\".\n","\n","![image.png](data:image/png;base64,)"],"metadata":{"id":"ohKRR8SVyR9A"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["You can delete your cell by pressing the delete icon on the top right of the cell:\n","![image.png](data:image/png;base64,)"],"metadata":{"id":"4_HWwkJr1j6j"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Here are some of the things that we can explore using the given data (You can choose as much as you can):\n","- Relationship between cancellation rates and the number of special requests or booking changes\n","- Frequency of Cancellations by Resort Type and the presence of children per guest\n","- Relation between the number of days in the waiting list to guest's cancellation\n","- Solo/Couple guest vs. Family guest cancellation rates\n","- Influence of lead time to guest cancellation\n","\n","Correspondingly, you may these methods to support your insights as well (if applicable):\n","- RFM analysis\n","- Hypothesis Testing"],"metadata":{"id":"Joi6AAffz7wn"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Additionally, you may add text cells if you wanted to provide some written explanation of the analysis that we make here."],"metadata":{"id":"Bh7oyOtt1ZKE"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# You may freely add cells and write code for this part"],"metadata":{"id":"-OIzyG3RzULQ"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Relationship between cancellation rates and the number of special requests or booking changes**\n","\n","---\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"KuGviknx16O0"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Calculate cancellation rates for different levels of special requests\n","special_requests_cancel_rate = data.groupby('special_requests')['is_canceled'].mean()\n","\n","# Visualize the cancellation rates\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n","sns.barplot(x=special_requests_cancel_rate.index, y=special_requests_cancel_rate.values, ax=ax)\n","ax.set_xlabel('Number of Special Requests')\n","ax.set_ylabel('Cancellation Rate')\n","ax.set_title('Cancellation Rate by Number of Special Requests')\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"33W9S9RW1LXC","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1685201431813,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":449,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"b49372a5-8128-4a4d-f30a-2c9b71f92f75"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Calculate cancellation rates for different levels of booking changes\n","booking_changes_cancel_rate = data.groupby('booking_changes')['is_canceled'].mean()\n","\n","# Visualize the cancellation rates\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n","sns.barplot(x=booking_changes_cancel_rate.index, y=booking_changes_cancel_rate.values, ax=ax)\n","ax.set_xlabel('Number of Booking Changes')\n","ax.set_ylabel('Cancellation Rate')\n","ax.set_title('Cancellation Rate by Number of Booking Changes')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"wKZdf9O71avX","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1685201491380,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":1118,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"500cc49d-8bb2-4690-efd5-fc24786a5470"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Frequency of Cancellations by Resort Type and the presence of children per guest**\n","\n","---\n","\n","\n","\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"DbgyPyff2FFo"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Create a contingency table\n","cancellation_table = pd.crosstab(data['hotel'], data['children'], values=data['is_canceled'], aggfunc='mean')\n","\n","# Visualize the contingency table\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n","sns.heatmap(cancellation_table, annot=True, cmap='Blues', fmt=\".2%\", cbar=True, ax=ax)\n","ax.set_xlabel('Presence of Children')\n","ax.set_ylabel('Resort Type')\n","ax.set_title('Cancellation Rate by Resort Type and Presence of Children')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"ZbPa1ejj1i9M","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1685202091806,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":1244,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"218ad80b-ca5b-4429-8047-50ac3bfc8b46"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Relation between the number of days in the waiting list to guest's cancellation**\n","\n","---\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"WBlY0vYX4MHF"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Filter the data for only canceled bookings\n","canceled_bookings = data[data['status'] == 'Canceled']\n","\n","# Create a scatter plot\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","plt.scatter(canceled_bookings['days_in_waiting_list'], canceled_bookings['status'], alpha=0.5)\n","\n","# Set the plot title and labels\n","plt.title(\"Relation between Days in Waiting List and Guest's Cancellation\")\n","plt.xlabel('Days in Waiting List')\n","plt.ylabel('Cancellation Status')\n","\n","# Show the plot\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"cuU1NTaf4QIM","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1685202319836,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":745,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"2dee514f-1c38-4cc1-95a5-97c015059802"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Solo/Couple guest vs. Family guest cancellation rates**\n","\n","---\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"_u6S808y44Sy"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Create a new column indicating whether the booking is solo/couple or family\n","data['guest_type'] = 'Solo/Couple'\n","data.loc[(data['adults'] + data['children']) > 1, 'guest_type'] = 'Family'\n","\n","# Calculate cancellation rates by guest type\n","cancellation_rates = data.groupby('guest_type')['is_canceled'].mean().reset_index()\n","\n","# Plot the cancellation rates\n","plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n","sns.barplot(data=cancellation_rates, x='guest_type', y='is_canceled')\n","plt.title(\"Cancellation Rates: Solo/Couple vs Family Guests\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Guest Type\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Cancellation Rate\")\n","\n","# Show the plot\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"ptCpWvV447c2","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1685202441762,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":942,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"2e45f2df-b4e4-4aff-cfe4-8c36bdab8991"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Influence of lead time to guest cancellation**\n","\n","---\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"Kyxg_dhQ5Obd"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Group data by lead time and calculate cancellation rate\n","cancellation_rate_lead_time = data.groupby('lead_time')['is_canceled'].mean().reset_index()\n","\n","# Plot the cancellation rate vs. lead time\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","sns.lineplot(data=cancellation_rate_lead_time, x='lead_time', y='is_canceled')\n","plt.title('Influence of Lead Time on Guest Cancellation')\n","plt.xlabel('Lead Time (days)')\n","plt.ylabel('Cancellation Rate')\n","\n","# Show the plot\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"IBruifO65SDc","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1685202512733,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":632,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"74299c5d-e358-4c99-984c-5f3e26f1b498"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Conclusions and Recommendations"],"metadata":{"id":"FhXng66greVE"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["For this part, we would have to provide overall conclusion based on the observations and insights that we made in the previous part.\n","\n","You may write down at least 2 sentences on what can you can observe in the data in general and what you can recommend to the management in order to resolve the increased booking cancellations given the results and insights that you've made so far.\n","\n","---"],"metadata":{"id":"PANUI_posK7b"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Based on the results of the analysis, there is a favorable relationship between the number of special requests and booking changes and the cancellation rates. Furthermore, when there are children present per guest, resort type hotels have more cancellation rates.\n","\n","I would recommend developing measures to streamline the special request and booking change processes, guaranteeing clear communication and accurate fulfillment, to address the rising booking cancellations. It would also be good to concentrate on knowing the special needs and wants of guests with children in resort-style hotels, and to provide tailored facilities and services to enhance their experience. Targeted marketing initiatives might be developed to attract and keep solo/couple guests, potentially lowering cancellation rates associated with family bookings. Furthermore, regular monitoring and analysis of lead time trends would allow for the implementation of adaptive cancellation policies to satisfy guests' shifting wants and concerns."],"metadata":{"id":"vF5WnzyOzAg9"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["---\n","\n","**END OF FILE**"],"metadata":{"id":"9A7GXLBfzFmf"}}]}